[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello,</p>\n<p>I just encountered this surprising behavior to me, of which a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> below:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">implicit_reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">trace: n : Nat</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ 2 * n = n + n</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">n2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n1</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">dsimp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trace_state</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">arith</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: `dsimp` made no progress -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">dsimp</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>f</code> is an implicit reducible function, which typically happens when <code>f</code> is part of a typeclass instance definition.</p>\n<p>When <code>f n</code> is under a match, then <code>dsimp</code> (or <code>simp</code>) will allow to unfold its definition, however when <code>f n</code> is not under a match, its definition is not unfolded.</p>\n<p>Is there any reason for this that I am missing, or is it a bug?</p>",
        "id": 601483313,
        "sender_full_name": "Théophile Wallez",
        "timestamp": 1781023016
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, testing on the lean playground reveals that it has been fixed in v4.31.0-rc2 <span aria-label=\"dotted line face\" class=\"emoji emoji-1fae5\" role=\"img\" title=\"dotted line face\">:dotted_line_face:</span></p>",
        "id": 601483675,
        "sender_full_name": "Théophile Wallez",
        "timestamp": 1781023120
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(I am curious what commit fixed this though? I would like to learn more about the fix but cannot find the corresponding commit between v4.30.0 and v4.31.0-rc2)</p>",
        "id": 601485854,
        "sender_full_name": "Théophile Wallez",
        "timestamp": 1781023677
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that was <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/13512\">lean4#13512</a>, or maybe something related</p>",
        "id": 601684946,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1781076525
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok thanks! I just tested nightly releases, which confirms that this might be the commit that fixed this.</p>\n<p>I see that this commit did not add regression test, do you think it would be possible to add the example above in the regression test suite of Lean? (ping <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"470149\">@Joachim Breitner</span>)</p>\n<p>This issue caused me great trouble inside a proof because it also interacts badly with grind, e.g.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">implicit_reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">n1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails with v4.30.0, succeds with v.4.31.0-rc2</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(because <code>grind</code> reduces the <code>f n</code> that is matched in the first line, but not the one that is projected in the second line)</p>",
        "id": 601722415,
        "sender_full_name": "Théophile Wallez",
        "timestamp": 1781083899
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you feel strongly enough about it to go through the trouble of creating a PR with a regression test, I'm happy to merge that if nobody beats me to it.</p>",
        "id": 602657760,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1781299840
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here it is: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14070\">lean4#14070</a></p>\n<p>Happy to do edits if the PR is not done properly :)</p>\n<p>(I do feel strong enough about it, because this issue caused me great trouble deep inside a complex proof, and I feel this behavior is in general undesirable!)</p>",
